{"case_id":"T5034","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","state","input_semantics"],"confidence":97,"affected_functions":["dictionary_fill","PList::Dictionary::Dictionary(plist_t, Node*)","Node::FromPlist"],"reason":"H0 fuzzes only the C parsing entry points `plist_from_bin` and `plist_from_xml`, then immediately calls `plist_free`. It never constructs the C++ `PList::Dictionary` wrapper whose constructor calls `dictionary_fill`. In S1, `dictionary_fill` mutates the actual member `_map` through a reference, exposing persistent C++ dictionary state populated from attacker-controlled keys and subnodes. That wrapper-conversion and populated-state surface is therefore absent from H0.","evidence":["`bplist_fuzzer.cc` calls only `plist_from_bin(..., &root_node)` followed by `plist_free(root_node)`.","`xplist_fuzzer.cc` calls only `plist_from_xml(..., &root_node)` followed by `plist_free(root_node)`.","`PList::Dictionary::Dictionary(plist_t node, Node* parent)` invokes `dictionary_fill(this, _map, _node)`.","S1 declares `dictionary_fill(Dictionary*, std::map<std::string,Node*> &map, plist_t)`, so assignments through `map[std::string(key)]` persist in `_map`.","Each dictionary subnode is converted through `Node::FromPlist(subnode, _this)`, a C++ conversion path not named or invoked by H0."],"recommended_action":"Add a C++ plist-wrapper fuzz target that parses binary and/or XML input, constructs the corresponding `PList::Dictionary` or general C++ `Node` wrapper for dictionary roots, exercises the populated dictionary state, and performs normal destruction under sanitizers."}
